Set up kubectl and eksctl

+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
Install or update kubectl

Step 1: Check if kubectl is installed
kubectl version --client

Step-2: Download the kubectl binary for your cluster’s Kubernetes version from Amazon S3. Kubernetes 1.36
curl -O https://s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/amazon-eks/1.36.2/2026-07-05/bin/linux/amd64/kubectl

Step-3: Apply execute permissions to the binary.
chmod +x ./kubectl

Step-4: Copy the binary to a folder in your PATH. If you have already installed a version of kubectl, then we recommend creating a $HOME/bin/kubectl and ensuring that $HOME/bin comes first in your $PATH. 
mkdir -p $HOME/bin && cp ./kubectl $HOME/bin/kubectl && export PATH=$HOME/bin:$PATH

Step-5: Add the $HOME/bin path to your shell initialization file so that it is configured when you open a shell.
echo 'export PATH=$HOME/bin:$PATH' >> ~/.bashrc

Step-6: check for the version
kubectl version

